We propose improved constructions of a verifiable homomorphic encryption (vHE) scheme supporting the class of linear and quadratic functions. Compared to prior works, our scheme is more efficient and flexible due to the full black-box use of a homomorphic encryption scheme. Furthermore, it can be composed with a class of commit-and-prove zk-SNARKs, and in the SIMD setting, supports efficient batching. Our technique is inspired by recent developments in zk-SNARKs, and its security holds in the algebraic group model.